<title>USA: G&amp;K names Hope to succeed Fink as CEO.</title>
<headline>G&amp;K names Hope to succeed Fink as CEO.</headline>
<dateline>MINNEAPOLIS 1996-10-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>G&amp;K Services Inc said Thursday it had named William Hope as chief executive officer, succeeding Richard Fink, who will step down on January 1.</p>
<p>Fink, who has been CEO since 1970 and chairman since 1981, will continue as chairman, G&amp;K said.  </p>
<p>Fink will retain responsibility for G&amp;K's manufacturing division and will continue to be involved in acquisitions and shareholder relations, the uniform supply company said.</p>
<p>Hope, G&amp;K's president and chief operating officer, has been with the company since 1965.</p>
<p>-- Chicago Newsdesk 312 408-8787</p>
